input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.
INFO: Loaded OpenCL library with dlopen.


On-device AI is like having a smart computer that can think and make decisions right where it's used, instead of sending all the data to the internet or a big server. Imagine if your phone could recognize a face or speak naturally just by using its own tiny computer, without needing a computer on the other side of the world. That's on-device AI. It helps with things like recognizing your face in photos, helping your smart speaker understand your voice, or even making decisions based on real-time data around you. It's like having a small brain in your pocket!

